From: nwrt Xiaomi 14 Pro integration
Subject: [PATCH] device: grab Xiaomi downstream rmnet ports as link ports

Mainline IPA exposes a lower-device relationship for dynamically created
QMAP netdevices. Xiaomi's downstream 6.1 rmnet driver does not expose that
sysfs relationship, so ModemManager mistakes the link for a new modem port and
restarts device probing while a bearer is waiting for it.

Treat only rmnet data netdevices explicitly assigned to the qcom-soc UID as link
ports. Other devices retain the upstream lower-device and WWAN detection.

--- a/src/mm-device.c
+++ b/src/mm-device.c
@@ -221,13 +221,19 @@ mm_device_grab_port (MMDevice       *self,
                      MMKernelDevice *kernel_port)
 {
     MMPortProbe    *probe;
     MMKernelDevice *lower_port;
+    gboolean        downstream_rmnet_link;
 
     if (mm_device_owns_port (self, kernel_port))
         return TRUE;
 
     lower_port = mm_kernel_device_peek_lower_device (kernel_port);
-    if (lower_port) {
+    downstream_rmnet_link =
+        (g_strcmp0 (mm_kernel_device_get_subsystem (kernel_port), "net") == 0 &&
+         (g_str_has_prefix (mm_kernel_device_get_name (kernel_port), "rmnet_data") ||
+          g_str_has_prefix (mm_kernel_device_get_name (kernel_port), "qmapmux")) &&
+         g_strcmp0 (mm_kernel_device_get_physdev_uid (kernel_port), "qcom-soc") == 0);
+    if (lower_port || downstream_rmnet_link) {
         g_autoptr(GError) error = NULL;
 
         /* No port probing done, at this point this is not something we require
